WEBVTT

00:03:29.156 --> 00:03:31.636
And so when I received these photos,

00:03:31.676 --> 00:03:35.476
I immediately knew that this could be
something very special indeed.

00:03:35.796 --> 00:03:37.636
But of course, just looking at photos,

00:03:37.676 --> 00:03:41.236
it's hard to know exactly whether
this is going to be something unique

00:03:41.276 --> 00:03:42.916
or is it just a few vertebrae?

00:03:44.636 --> 00:03:48.876
After speaking to fellow marine
reptile expert Dr. Mark Evans,

00:03:48.916 --> 00:03:51.236
who was also sent details of the find,

00:03:51.276 --> 00:03:53.876
we decided to visit the site in February.

00:03:53.876 --> 00:03:57.036
And I led a mini excavation,

00:03:57.076 --> 00:03:59.796
a bit of an exploratory dig
to see what we could uncover.